{{Protection}}{{Title Icon}}
Ranked is a competitive mode unlocked from the [[Trophy Road]] at 5000 [[Trophies]]. It replaced [[Power League]] in the [[Version History#Patch notes: Ranked Update 27/02/24|February 2024 update]]. Players can promote to higher Ranks or drop to lower Ranks based on the outcome of each match. Only Power 11 Brawlers can be played. Every month, a season ends and the next one begins, and every player's Rank is reduced when a new season begins. [[Trophies]] cannot be gained or lost in Ranked.

==Gameplay==
In a Ranked match, players will play a random 3v3 mode on a random map. In {{Color|93f|Mythic I}} and above, both teams have a team captain, which is either decided by the player with the highest Elo or by the host of the game room (when playing in a team). Team captains get the last pick in the drafting phase.

From {{Color|f90|Bronze I}} to {{Color|fc0|Gold III}}, like [[Mega Pig]] matches, each player picks a Brawler that has not already been picked by a teammate and equips any Star Powers, Gadgets, and Gears without any extra delay prior to starting the match. If a player does not pick a Brawler within the 22-second time limit, the match is cancelled and all players are sent to the lobby. Players can also suggest a Brawler to a teammate, or preselect a Brawler which is visible to teammates. Preselecting may be wise as players can change their loadout because the match starts as soon as all players have picked a Brawler.

From {{Color|3cf|Diamond I}} to {{Color|3cf|Diamond III}}, each player starts by banning Brawlers, preventing anyone on either team from picking them in the selection phase. During the ban phase, players can only see the bans of their own team, and players from the same team cannot ban the same Brawler more than once. Bans can also be preselected. If the 22.5-second timer runs out, a random Brawler will be banned if no selection was attempted. Then players pick as normal and the match starts. It is required to have at least 12 Power 11 Brawlers to queue.

Starting from {{Color|93f|Mythic I}}, like [[Power League]], Ranked matches are formatted as a best-of-3-tournament where the first team to win 2 rounds is the winner. If rounds end in a draw, a winner is automatically decided after the third round; there is no rematch in this case. A coin flip occurs once the matchmaking is complete that determines which team gets the first pick. After the ban phase, each player chooses the Brawlers one by one, with each player allotted 22 seconds to choose their Brawler. If the blue team picks first, Brawlers are picked in the following sequence: {{Color|55f|Blue 3}}, {{Color|f55|Red 3}}, {{Color|f55|Red 2}}, {{Color|55f|Blue 2}}, {{Color|55f|Blue 1}}, {{Color|f55|Red 1}}. Additionally, after all Brawlers are picked, all players have 17 seconds to choose Star Powers, Gadgets, and Gears, if applicable. They also have the option to swap Brawlers with a teammate.

==Ranks==
Ranks range from {{Color|f90|Bronze I}} to {{Color|666|Pro}}. Higher Ranks become increasingly more difficult to progress as the skill level of everyone in the match increases. Higher Ranks also are more punishing with Elo loss when losing a match. {{Color|666|Pro}} is the final Rank, however progression does not end there, players can still earn more Elo to compete on the Ranked leaderboards.

