==Reputation Meter==
Each player has an individual Reputation Meter ranging from 0 to 25. Reputation drops when a player leaves a match too early. They will recover Reputation however, when finishing matches without getting disconnected and reported. When their Reputation has dropped to 9 or less, they will get a yellow card, warning them that more penalties will result in suspension from Ranked matches. When their Reputation has dropped to 0, they will get banned from playing Ranked for 30 minutes and are placed at 10 Reputation. At higher Ranks, players will also have their Elo reduced (e.g. losing 35 Elo at Masters II). Ranked Reputation is seperate from [[Trophies|Trophy]] Reputation.

Reputation changes based on the following factors:
*-10 - Getting disconnected for inactivity during a match
*-15 - Getting disconnected during the selection phase
* +1 - Finishing a match without getting disconnected and not getting reported (matches above Mythic still give +1 rep)

===Reporting System===
The Reporting System is a feature that allows the player to report other players from their own and the enemy team at the end of a Ranked match for intentionally disrupting the playing experience for everyone involved. There are 3 types of report that can be made, which are ''Bad Random'', ''Grief Play'', and ''Cheating''. Reporting does not affect Reputation directly, but submits the match for manual review. You will recieve a message in your inbox "''An action has been taken against a player you have reported.''" if the report was successful.

==History==
*On 27/02/24, Ranked was added to the game and replaced [[Power League]].
*On 04/03/24, server changes were applied to improve matchmaking.
*On 06/03/24, fixed an issue with players teaming up in Duos.
*On 25/03/24, Solo players facing teams now receive Elo as if they are playing against similarly ranked players. Wins now always give a minimum amount of Elo, and the maximum amount of Elo gained for losses has been reduced. Made general changes to Elo distribution to reduce inflation.
*On 23/04/24, matchmaking will now favor teams playing against other teams. Elo gain for solo players will now consider the team average Elo against the opposing team's. Adjusted the Elo gain in Legendary II up to Masters. Rank Boost will now give a higher boost depending on how high you reached in the previous Ranked season. Players in the Bronze to Gold Ranks now have a higher chance of getting Modifiers in their matches. Probability of getting Modifiers for players in Masters was reduced.
*On 25/04/24, fixed Ranked Boost stopping one Rank lower than it should. Ranked Boost was rebalanced: Bronze (no boost), Silver (10%), Gold (20%), Diamond (30%), Mythic (50%), Legendary (75%), Masters (100%).
*On 03/05/24, Second Wind Modifier now has a 1% chance of being selected. Fixed the Ranked Star not appearing when the player gets to the same Rank twice or more.
*On 12/09/24, fixed a bug making matchmaking longer than supposed.
*On 04/10/24, fixed the issue that caused the Ranked Boost, Ranked Battle Cards and Previous Ranked season leaderboards to be missing. Fixed an issue where the Malicious Mandy skin was unavailable in Ranked Starr Drops. The Malicious Mandy skin could be obtained for free by reaching Legendary I during Ranked Season 26.
*On 29/10/24, lowered Elo gain and minimum Elo gain for Legendary III and Masters (from +25 to +10), and increased Elo loss and minimum Elo loss for Masters.
*On 31/10/24, fixed unusual behavior with Win Streak while playing Ranked.
*On 25/02/25, Ranked was reworked, and the Pro Pass was added. Ranked seasons now start on the third Thursday of each month. Winning Ranked matches and ranking up now awards Pro Pass XP. Added Masters II and III, and the Pro Rank. Bronze and Silver now takes 250 Elo, Legendary takes 750 Elo, and Masters takes 1000 Elo to advance each Rank. Adjusted floor protection for Mythic and up. The Elo distribution was changed. Reduced Ranked Boost to 10%. Teaming up in higher Ranks is more restrictive. Matchmaking no longer increases Elo search range outside of your Rank restriction. Rank reset now resets players by 6 Ranks above Diamond I. Mythic and above now requires Power 11 Brawlers. Modifiers were removed. Each season, 3 maxed Brawlers are available for everyone in Ranked. Added Pro Pass XP in Ranked Starr Drops. A new set of Ranked Battle Cards were added.
*On 03/03/25, [[Bounty]] was added back to the rotation and the number of maps for each mode was increased from 3 to 4, increasing the total number of maps from 15 to 24.
*On 04/03/25, fixed various visual issues related to Ranked.
*On 12/03/25, fixed various visual issues related to Ranked.
*On 17/04/25, [[Hot Zone]] was replaced by [[Heist]] in the rotation. [[Brawl Hockey]] was replaced by [[Cleaning Duty]].
*On 30/04/25, fixed a bug preventing Gadget selection for free maxed out Brawlers if the player already owned one.
*On 15/05/25, [[Cleaning Duty]] was replaced by [[Hot Zone]] in the rotation.
*On 19/06/25, Ranked seasons will now have one of the modes selected as a featured mode for that season, which will put additional maps of that mode in the map rotation.
*On 24/06/25, Elo loss from Legendary III and above was reduced to mostly flat Elo. The time limit to meet same opponents was reduced from 12 hours to 1 hour.
*On 17/07/25, Masters and above can only queue solo. 
*On 23/07/25, fixed a bug with the Ranked leaderboard.
*On 13/08/25, fixed incorrect end-of-battle screen stats for matches below Mythic. Fixed a bug where Ranked Starr Drops were not working properly and were only rewarding Bling and Pro Pass XP.
*On 17/09/25, fixed a bug where players were stuck in matchmaking.
*On 25/02/26, fixed an edge case that could cause a crash in the loadout screen.
*On 16/04/26, Trial Brawlers with [[Buffies]] will also have them during the season.
*On 22/04/26, the limit of 10 reports per day was removed.
*On 03/11/26, many changes were applied to Ranked:
**'''Ranked restrictions''': Ranked unlocks at 5000 Trophies (from 1000). Only Brawlers at Power 11 can be picked (from 9). Diamond requires 12 eligible Brawlers (from 9). 6 Trial Brawlers are available each season (from 3).
**'''Draft screen''': The draft screen was rebuilt from the ground up! More filter options and a search bar was added. The ability to suggest bans, swap during the selection phase, use quick chat, use pins, and switch skin during final preparation was added.
**'''Elo/Rank changes''': Gain more Elo for a 2-0, and lose less for a 1-2. The Elo system was changed (more details TBD). Pro no longer unlocks the esports button.
**'''Season changes''': Ranked reset was decreased to 2 Ranks (from 6). Changes to Ranked boost (more details TBD). A new set of Battle Cards were added, with each Battle Card maxing out at 9 times (from 7). Player icons and pins were added for reaching Ranks for the first time. Pro Pass XP was increased to 60 per win (from 50), and the weekly limit was increased to 1200 (from 1000).
**'''QoL''': A new stats button and the play again button was added to end screens. Spectating was changed to spectate the full match instead of just 1 round. The color of Masters and Pro was changed. New Rank icons and sound effects were added.

